course: dictionary
lesson: 8536
title: The sawfish and its saw
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sawfish is a real animal, and its name tells you what it looks like. Read the words around a new word to learn what it means. «A sawfish is a ray with a long flat saw edged with tooth-like points» tells you the sawfish has a saw, and the saw is not for cutting wood.
explain: The sawfish uses its saw to stun fish, which means knocking them dazed or unable to move. «It swings the saw» shows it is a moving tool. «The saw also feels the tiny electric signals of hidden prey» shows the saw can sense food that is hidden, so a sawfish can find food even when it cannot see it.
explain: Scientists say an animal is adapted when its body fits its home. A sawfish lives in warm coastal waters and rivers, for example in northern Australia, and its saw helps it hunt there. Look for clues like this in every text you read.
fact: A sawfish is a large ray, a flat fish related to sharks.
fact: Its long flat snout is edged with sharp teeth, like the teeth of a saw.
fact: A sawfish swings its saw to stun small fish, slash them, and dig for food in mud.
fact: The saw can sense the tiny electric signals made by hidden prey.
fact: Sawfish are critically endangered, often caught by accident in fishing nets. Smalltooth and largetooth are two kinds of sawfish.
exercise: «Sawfish are critically endangered, mainly because their saws tangle in fishing nets.» What does endangered mean here? | Good at catching fish | Found only in deep caves | Very large and heavy | *In danger of dying out
exercise: What is a sawfish related to? | Crabs | Whales | Eagles | *Sharks
exercise: «It swings the saw to stun fish.» What does stun mean? | To cook | *To make dazed or unable to move | To count | To hide
test: Where do sawfish live? | In dry deserts | In cold, deep ice water | Only in high mountain lakes | *In warm coastal waters and rivers, for example in northern Australia
test: Why are sawfish critically endangered? | *They are often caught by accident in fishing nets | Their saws are too heavy to swim with | They are too small to be seen | They have no teeth left to eat with
exam: «The saw also feels the tiny electric signals of hidden prey.» How does a sawfish find hidden food? | It looks for light at night | It listens for singing | *Its saw senses the tiny electric signals the prey makes | It follows the smell of bread
